       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum.\n\n- **Single dose:** The usual maximum is 800 mg per dose. 1600 mg is double that.\n- **Daily total:** The maximum for prescription use is 3,200 mg/day. For an inpatient, 2,400 to 3,200 mg/day is typical. 6,400 mg/day greatly raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It also adds no extra analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, because the effect plateaus.\n\nNormal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change those limits.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum standard dose\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed** for pain or fever\n- **1600 mg total per day,** for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and add a note with the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with that note, though pharmacy will likely contact you about it."
      }
